@@ -9,13 +9,29 @@ persistence is an in-memory repository behind a small interface.
   append-only `Ledger`; never stored. Only receipts, adjustments (counts,
   write-offs) and shipments write to the ledger.
 - **Allocated** — units promised to `PLACED` orders that have not shipped yet.
-- **Available** — `on_hand - allocated`, floored at zero. This is what new
-  orders may take.
+- **Held** — units held by `ACTIVE` reservations that have not expired yet.
+- **Available** — `on_hand - allocated - held`, floored at zero. This is what
+  new orders and reservations may take.
 
 Order lifecycle: `place_order` (allocates, all lines or nothing) →
 `ship_order` (writes `SHIPMENT` ledger entries) or `cancel_order` (releases
 the allocation).
 
+Reservation lifecycle (checkout holds stock before payment):
+
+- `reserve(warehouse, items, idempotency_key)` → `ACTIVE`. Each line holds
+  what is available, up to what was asked; lines with nothing available are
+  dropped. Fails with `InsufficientStock` only if no line can hold anything.
+  Holds last 20 minutes (`reservation_ttl` on the service).
+- Same key and same request (warehouse + requested items) returns the
+  existing reservation as it is now; a different request with a used key
+  raises `IdempotencyConflict`. Failed calls do not consume the key.
+- `confirm_reservation` → `CONFIRMED`, places a `PLACED` order for exactly the
+  held units. Repeating it returns the same order.
+- `release_reservation` → `RELEASED`; a no-op on `RELEASED`/`EXPIRED`.
+- A hold is `EXPIRED` from `expires_at` on. Expiry is evaluated against the
+  clock on every read; there is no sweep job.
+
 ## Conventions
 
 - All time comes from an injected `Clock` (`FixedClock` in tests). Never call
